# ---- internal docs -------------------------------------------------------
# The repo is public. These are working notes, business decisions, unsent
# letters, API findings from an employee's access, and a candid account of
# how the project is run. None of it is secret exactly, but none of it is
# addressed to strangers either, and some of it (the Decky submission
# letter, the free-user business decision, the internal API notes) reads
# very differently without the room it was written in.
#
# Kept locally, ignored here. docs/install-flow.md stays in the repo because
# it documents what a user is asked to run.
